Liquify began as a clone of that project and a large part of its foundation is
derived from it, with modifications. That includes, but is not limited to:

  - the rounded-rectangle signed distance field, its gradient, and the
    refraction and rim-highlight AGSL programs (internal/Shaders.kt)
  - the Backdrop interface, the backdrop implementations and the layer capture
  - the backdrop effect scope and the blur, colour-filter, lens and raw
    render-effect operations built on it
  - the glass draw node, and the highlight, shadow and inner-shadow nodes
  - the highlight styles, the shadow and inner-shadow value types, and the
    supporting internal helpers (paint, outline, layer recording, inverse layer
    scope, shape provider, render-effect composition)
  - the press/drag tracking, the damped drag animation and the drag gesture
    detector, which in the original are part of its sample application

Every file derived from that project carries a notice to that effect at the top
of the file, as required by section 4(b) of the License.

Work original to Liquify includes the merged distance-field pass and the group
renderer that produces the liquid merging effect, the gradient blur, the
material presets and application-wide material theming, the transitions, and the
consolidated `liquify` modifier API.

